module

public import CompositionAlgebras.Composition.NormEquivalence
public import CompositionAlgebras.Composition.RankOneTwoFourEight
public import CompositionAlgebras.LGRing.ConstantRank

/-!
# Unital norm equivalences of quadratic algebras are isomorphisms (`GPR 23.4(b)`)

A **quadratic algebra** over a commutative ring `k` is a unital `k`-algebra that is finitely
generated projective of rank two as a `k`-module (`GPR 16.4`). `GPR 23.4(b)` says that a unital
norm equivalence from one quadratic algebra onto another — a linear bijection carrying `1` to `1`
and the norm to the norm (`GPR 23.1`) — is an isomorphism. This file proves it in that generality:
over an **arbitrary** commutative ring, with no LG, nontriviality, regularity or characteristic
hypothesis. It removes the global generator that `Composition/NormEquivalence.lean` needs.

## The proof

This is `GPR`'s proof. Multiplicativity is an equation in `B`, so it may be checked after base
change to the localization `k_𝔪` at every maximal ideal
(`ConicAlgebra.eq_of_forall_localization_maximal`), and a unital norm equivalence base changes to
one (`QuadraticMap.IsometryEquiv.baseChangeOfProjective`). Over `k_𝔪` the unit is unimodular
(`GPR 16.7`), so it splits off a free summand `k_𝔪 ⊗ A ≃ k_𝔪 × N`; the complement `N` is
projective of rank one over a local ring, hence free on a single `u`, and `k_𝔪 ⊗ A = k_𝔪[u]`.
Multiplication in `k[u]` has only the structure constants `t(u)` and `n(u)` (`GPR 19.8`), and a
unital norm equivalence preserves both (`GPR 23.2`), so the engine
`ConicAlgebra.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement` applies.

The generator is produced over any LG ring, not only over a local one
(`ConicAlgebra.exists_forall_mem_adjoinElement_of_isLGRing_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two`), since that is
where constant-rank projectives are free (`GPR 11.24`); no composition hypothesis is needed.

## How the statement matches `GPR 23.4(b)`

`GPR 16.4` makes a quadratic algebra conic by Cayley–Hamilton, with `n(x) = det(L_x)` and
`t(x) = tr(L_x)`. The statements here instead take **arbitrary** conic structures `C` on `A` and
`D` on `B`. This loses nothing: a finitely generated projective algebra carries at most one conic
norm (`ConicAlgebra.norm_eq_of_projective`, `GPR 16.16`), so whatever conic structure is supplied,
its norm is the norm of `GPR 16.4`, and "`e` is a unital norm equivalence" means exactly what it
means in `GPR`. Only `A` is assumed finitely generated projective of constant rank two; for `B` this
follows from the linear equivalence, so `B` is only assumed to be conic. Neither algebra is assumed
associative or commutative — both are consequences (`GPR 16.4`).

⚠ The existence half of `GPR 16.4`, that every unital algebra which is projective of rank two
admits a conic norm, is not formalized here; the conic structure is an input.

## Main results

* `ConicAlgebra.exists_forall_mem_adjoinElement_of_isLGRing_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two` : over an LG
  ring, a finitely generated projective conic algebra of constant rank two is `k[u]` for some `u`.
* `ConicAlgebra.map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two` : **`GPR 23.4(b)`**.
* `ConicAlgebra.isomorphic_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two` : the same, as
  `ConicAlgebra.Isomorphic`.
* `ConicAlgebra.map_mul_iff_norm_map_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two` : **`GPR 23.4`** for quadratic
  algebras, both directions: a unital linear equivalence is multiplicative if and only if it
  preserves the norm.

## References

* [GPR] Garibaldi, Petersson, Racine, *Albert Algebras over Commutative Rings*, 11.24, 16.4, 16.7,
  16.16, 19.8, 23.1, 23.2, 23.4.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace ConicAlgebra

variable {k : Type u} {A : Type v} [CommRing k] [NonAssocRing A] [Module k A]
  [SMulCommClass k A A] [IsScalarTower k A A] [Module.Finite k A] [Module.Projective k A]
  {B : Type w} [NonAssocRing B] [Module k B] [SMulCommClass k B B] [IsScalarTower k B B]

/-- **The local step of `GPR 23.4(b)`, over an LG ring.** A finitely generated projective conic
algebra of constant rank two over an LG ring is generated by one element: `A = k[u]`
(`GPR 19.8`).

The unit is unimodular (`GPR 16.7`), so a functional `l` with `l 1 = 1` splits `A ≃ k × ker l`,
and `ker l` is projective of constant rank one, hence free (`GPR 11.24`); its generator is `u`.
`GPR` uses this over a local ring, extending `1` to a basis of `A`. No composition, regularity or
nontriviality hypothesis is needed. -/
theorem exists_forall_mem_adjoinElement_of_isLGRing_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two (C : ConicAlgebra k A)
    (hLG : IsLGRing k) (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2) :
    ∃ u : A, ∀ x : A, x ∈ C.adjoinElement u := by
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial k with hk | hk
  · have : Subsingleton A := Module.subsingleton k A
    exact ⟨0, fun x ↦ (C.mem_adjoinElement_iff 0 x).mpr ⟨0, 0, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := Module.isUnimodular_iff.mp C.isUnimodular_one
  set e := LinearMap.equivProdKerOfApplyEqOne l 1 hl
  have : Module.Finite k (LinearMap.ker l) := Module.Finite.of_linearEquiv_prod e
  have : Module.Projective k (LinearMap.ker l) := Module.Projective.of_linearEquiv_prod e
  have hker : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) (LinearMap.ker l) = fun _ ↦ 1 := by
    have hM := Module.rankAtStalk_eq_of_equiv e
    rw [Module.rankAtStalk_prod, Module.rankAtStalk_self] at hM
    funext p
    have := congrFun (hM.symm.trans hA) p
    simp only [Pi.add_apply, Pi.one_apply] at this
    omega
  have : Module.Free k (LinearMap.ker l) :=
    Module.free_of_isLGRing_of_rankAtStalk_eq hLG 1 _ hker
  have hfin : Module.finrank k (LinearMap.ker l) = 1 := by
    obtain ⟨p⟩ : Nonempty (PrimeSpectrum k) := inferInstance
    have := congrFun hker p
    rwa [Module.rankAtStalk_eq_finrank_of_free] at this
  let b := Module.finBasisOfFinrankEq k (LinearMap.ker l) hfin
  refine ⟨(b 0 : A), fun x ↦ (C.mem_adjoinElement_iff _ x).mpr ?_⟩
  have hx : x - l x • (1 : A) ∈ LinearMap.ker l := by
    simp [LinearMap.mem_ker, hl]
  refine ⟨l x, b.repr ⟨_, hx⟩ 0, ?_⟩
  have hsum := b.sum_repr ⟨_, hx⟩
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_one] at hsum
  have hcoe : b.repr ⟨_, hx⟩ 0 • (b 0 : A) = x - l x • 1 := congrArg Subtype.val hsum
  rw [hcoe]
  abel

/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)`.** A unital norm equivalence from a quadratic algebra onto a conic algebra is
multiplicative, over an arbitrary commutative ring.

Here `A` is finitely generated projective of constant rank two, i.e. quadratic in the sense of
`GPR 16.4`; the target `B` need only be conic, since finite generation, projectivity and rank pass
to it along `e`. The conic structures are arbitrary, which is no loss: on a finitely generated
projective algebra the conic norm is unique (`ConicAlgebra.norm_eq_of_projective`), so it is the
norm `det(L_x)` of `GPR 16.4`.

Following `GPR`, the equation is checked at each localization `k_𝔪`, where `k_𝔪 ⊗ A = k_𝔪[u]`
(`ConicAlgebra.exists_forall_mem_adjoinElement_of_isLGRing_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two`) and
multiplication in `k_𝔪[u]` is determined by `t(u)` and `n(u)` (`GPR 19.8`), both preserved by a
unital norm equivalence (`GPR 23.2`). -/
theorem map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two (C : ConicAlgebra k A)
    (D : ConicAlgebra k B) (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2)
    (e : C.norm.IsometryEquiv D.norm) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) (x y : A) :
    e (x * y) = e x * e y := by
  have : Module.Finite k B := Module.Finite.equiv e.toLinearEquiv
  have : Module.Projective k B := Module.Projective.of_equiv' e.toLinearEquiv
  refine eq_of_forall_localization_maximal (k := k) _ _ fun P _ ↦ ?_
  let S := Localization.AtPrime P
  have hSrank : Module.rankAtStalk (R := S) (S ⊗[k] A) = fun _ ↦ 2 := by
    funext q
    rw [Module.rankAtStalk_baseChange, hA]
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := (C.baseChangeOfProjective S)
    |>.exists_forall_mem_adjoinElement_of_isLGRing_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two
      (isLGRing_of_isLocalRing S) hSrank
  let eS := QuadraticMap.IsometryEquiv.baseChangeOfProjective (A := S) C.norm D.norm e
  have h1S : eS (1 : S ⊗[k] A) = 1 := congrArg ((1 : S) ⊗ₜ[k] ·) h1
  have h := map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_forall_mem_adjoinElement
    (C.baseChangeOfProjective S) (D.baseChangeOfProjective S) eS h1S hu (1 ⊗ₜ x) (1 ⊗ₜ y)
  rw [← one_tmul_mul] at h
  exact h.trans (one_tmul_mul S (e x) (e y)).symm

/-- **`GPR 23.4(b)`, as an isomorphism.** A unital norm equivalence from a quadratic algebra onto a
conic algebra is an isomorphism of conic algebras, over an arbitrary commutative ring. -/
theorem isomorphic_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two (C : ConicAlgebra k A)
    (D : ConicAlgebra k B) (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2)
    (e : C.norm.IsometryEquiv D.norm) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) : C.Isomorphic D :=
  ⟨e, h1, map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two C D hA e h1⟩

/-- **`GPR 23.4` for quadratic algebras, both directions.** Let `A` be finitely generated
projective of constant rank two and `e : A ≃ₗ[k] B` a linear equivalence with `e 1 = 1`. Then `e`
is multiplicative if and only if it carries the norm of `C` to the norm of `D`.

Forwards is `GPR 23.4(a)` (`ConicAlgebra.norm_map_of_linearEquiv`) and holds in every rank;
backwards is `GPR 23.4(b)`, where rank two is used. -/
theorem map_mul_iff_norm_map_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two (C : ConicAlgebra k A) (D : ConicAlgebra k B)
    (hA : Module.rankAtStalk (R := k) A = fun _ ↦ 2) (e : A ≃ₗ[k] B) (h1 : e (1 : A) = 1) :
    (∀ x y, e (x * y) = e x * e y) ↔ ∀ x, D.norm (e x) = C.norm x :=
  ⟨fun hmul x ↦ norm_map_of_linearEquiv C D e h1 hmul x, fun hnorm ↦
    map_mul_of_isometryEquiv_map_one_of_rankAtStalk_eq_two C D hA
      { toLinearEquiv := e, map_app' := hnorm } h1⟩

end ConicAlgebra
